From a6d594364e8ef9c2324fc4edd9935bed20125ccf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Tue, 7 Apr 2026 22:51:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] DisplayPowerController: disable ColorFade on broken vendor
 HWC blobs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

certain vendor HWC implementations — confirmed for the mediatek
mtk_common HWC HAL on MT6789 — hang indefinitely inside the
BLASTBufferQueue.nativeCreate() call made from ColorFade.prepare()
when it lands while an HWC setPowerMode() is still propagating
through the panel init sequence (lcm_prepare / mtk_session_set_mode).
the binder call into surfaceflinger sits behind the HWC main-thread
work, never returns, and after 60s the watchdog kills system_server
with a stack trace pointing at:

  BLASTBufferQueue.nativeCreate
  ColorFade.createSurfaceControl
  ColorFade.prepare
  DisplayPowerState.prepareColorFade
  DisplayPowerController.animateScreenStateChange

system_server respawns, hits the same code path, hangs again, and
the device never finishes booting. user 0 stays in BOOTING state,
ACTION_BOOT_COMPLETED never broadcasts, every task stays sleeping,
every window stays hidden, surfaceflinger composes nothing and the
panel appears black.

the bug is in the closed-source vendor HWC blob, which we cannot
fix on a GSI build. work around it at the framework layer by
checking ro.hardware.hwcomposer at DisplayPowerController construct
time and forcing mColorFadeEnabled=false on a small blocklist of
known-broken HALs. starts with mtk_common since that's the one we
have a confirmed reproduction for. devices with other HWC HALs
keep their fade animation unchanged.

the only user-visible loss on affected devices is the brief
fade-in/out when the screen turns on or off.
---
 .../server/display/DisplayPowerController.java  | 17 ++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/DisplayPowerController.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/DisplayPowerController.java
index 54d2cd7cc..8dd9fafd8 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/DisplayPowerController.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/DisplayPowerController.java
@@ -680,9 +680,18 @@ final class DisplayPowerController implements AutomaticBrightnessController.Call
 
         setUpAutoBrightness(context, handler);
 
+        // some vendor HWC blobs (e.g. mediatek mtk_common) hang inside
+        // BLASTBufferQueue.nativeCreate when ColorFade.prepare runs alongside
+        // an in-flight HWC setPowerMode, blocking system_server until watchdog
+        // kills it and putting the device into a crash-respawn loop that never
+        // completes boot. detect those HALs at runtime and force ColorFade
+        // off so the device can actually boot.
+        boolean colorFadeBlocklisted =
+                "mtk_common".equals(SystemProperties.get("ro.hardware.hwcomposer", ""));
         mColorFadeEnabled = mInjector.isColorFadeEnabled()
                 && !resources.getBoolean(
-                  com.android.internal.R.bool.config_displayColorFadeDisabled);
+                  com.android.internal.R.bool.config_displayColorFadeDisabled)
+                && !colorFadeBlocklisted;
         mColorFadeFadesConfig = resources.getBoolean(
                 R.bool.config_animateScreenLights);
 
@@ -2351,7 +2360,8 @@ final class DisplayPowerController implements AutomaticBrightnessController.Call
             mPendingScreenOff = false;
         }
 
-        if (mFlags.isEnsureColorFadeWhenTurningOnEnabled()
+        if (mColorFadeEnabled
+                && mFlags.isEnsureColorFadeWhenTurningOnEnabled()
                 && ((mPowerState.getScreenState() == Display.STATE_OFF)
                 && target != Display.STATE_OFF)) {
             // ensure ColorFade is present.
@@ -2360,7 +2370,8 @@ final class DisplayPowerController implements AutomaticBrightnessController.Call
                     mColorFadeFadesConfig ? ColorFade.MODE_FADE : ColorFade.MODE_WARM_UP);
         }
 
-        if (mDisplayBlanksAfterDozeConfig
+        if (mColorFadeEnabled
+                && mDisplayBlanksAfterDozeConfig
                 && Display.isDozeState(mPowerState.getScreenState())
                 && !Display.isDozeState(target)) {
             // Skip the screen off animation and add a black surface to hide the
-- 
